# Senior Financial Crime Intelligence Analyst - Crypto
UK
**About us:**
BVNK is the stablecoin-powered financial stack for enterprises. We're now part of Mastercard, and together we're building a network for every form of money – one that delivers more reach, more capability and more choice.
We enable businesses to build financial products, unlock new markets, and move money in seconds across 130+ countries, with 40+ licenses for fiat and digital assets globally. Processing billions annually, we empower enterprises worldwide to send, receive, convert, and settle stablecoins and fiat seamlessly through a single integration.
**Our mission is to accelerate global money movement, and we're assembling a world-class team to make it happen.**
Trusted by industry leaders like Corpay, Worldpay, Deel, and Flywire, we deliver the infrastructure that makes new forms of money usable within the financial systems customers already rely on today.
By combining Mastercard's global payment reach and trusted networks with BVNK's stablecoin infrastructure, we're building the trusted operating layer for the evolution of money movement, helping customers participate in emerging digital networks without having to rebuild their businesses around every new innovation.
We're a diverse team spread across EMEA, North America, and APAC, with a shared belief that stablecoins are the new infrastructure layer for financial services, and that BVNK is at the forefront of this shift.
We're incredibly honored to have been recognized by:
* CNBC World's Top Fintech Companies (2026)
* FXC Intelligence Top 100 Cross-border Payment Companies (2026)
* Newsweek's The Top 100 Global Most Loved Workplaces (three years running, most recently 2025)
* LinkedIn as one of the Top 20 Startups in the UK (2025)
**About this role in the team:**
**We are currently looking for a Senior Crypto Analyst to join our fast growing FCI team**
As a Senior Financial Crime Intelligence Analyst, you'll play a key role in handling screening and transaction monitoring alerts to prevent bad actors from processing transactions through BVNK. You’ll also conduct in-depth analysis and thorough investigations to address complex and varied financial crime threats. You’ll be taking ownership of cases triggered by BVNK’s financial crime systems and controls, focussing primarily on BVNK’s digital assets offering, and mitigating financial crime risks for BVNK. While this role focuses on BVNK’s digital assets offering, your cases will inevitably crossover with the world of fiat currency and you’ll have the opportunity to support cutting-edge investigations in fiat and digital assets. We are seeking a candidate who can commit to a full-time schedule working from 9 a.m. to 6 p.m. (CEST).
We are looking for a team player; someone who is adaptable and enjoys solving complex problems in a constantly changing environment. You must be adept at managing competing priorities, and work well in a highly demanding environment. You will be comfortable delivering high quality investigations at pace, and presenting your findings and recommendations to senior stakeholders.
**As a Senior Financial Crime Intelligence Analyst, your day-to-day role will be varied, but will include tasks such as:**
* Reviewing of sanctions and watchlist screening alerts on entities and individuals on relevant lists;
* Management of end-to-end financial crime investigations stemming from BVNK’s transaction monitoring system, Trade Surveillance, payment screening tools, blockchain analytics provider, and other triggers;
* Identify opportunities to improve workflows and business processes through the effective use of AI tools and automation;
* Receiving escalations from, and providing coaching to, more junior team members;
* Drafting of Suspicious Activity Reports (SARs) for submission to the relevant authorities;
* Working closely with colleagues responsible for BVNK’s transaction monitoring systems; identifying and testing changes to the rules in our transaction monitoring system;
* Seeking out and escalating opportunities to enhance BVNK’s control environment.
**We’d love to hear from you if:**
* You have at least 3 years’ experience in crypto transaction monitoring within a regulated institution or digital assets setting. Experience in a B2B context is essential, as we are primarily a B2B business. Familiarity with B2C environments is a plus, and experience across both crypto and fiat transaction monitoring environments would be advantageous;
* You have experience reviewing sanctions and watchlist screening alerts, within a regulated institution or digital asset setting;
* You have experience using tools such as Chainalysis, Elliptic, or TRM (or equivalent). Any blockchain related investigative certifications are desirable but not required;
* Experience leveraging AI tools and technologies to streamline processes, automate routine tasks, and drive operational improvements;
* Strong knowledge of AML/CTF regulations, financial crime typologies, and risk-based compliance frameworks is required;
* Knowledge of Trade Surveillance would be an asset;
* You’ve drafted and submitted Suspicious Activity Reports (SARs);
* You’re a motivated and proactive individual contributor, who takes pride in the quality of your work;
* You’re comfortable working in a fast-paced, evolving and demanding environment, often with competing priorities;
* You’re happy working with a high degree of autonomy and managing evolving priorities to deliver against the team's strategy;
* You have an interest in digital assets, and are looking for an opportunity to expand your knowledge in this space;
* You have exceptional written and verbal English;
**What you can expect from us:**
* Fair and **competitive salary** at every stage of your growth
* **Flexible working** hours, with hybrid working at its heart
* A **culture** built on passionate growth-minded people
* A **flexible approach to holiday**
* Opportunities to travel to our **offices around the world**
* An **open and creative environment** where you can help us define the future of BVNK, its culture, and its opportunity sets
*At BVNK, we are focused on building a diverse and inclusive team. While you may not meet all of our requirements, we’d encourage you to apply if you meet the majority of our expectations. You may be a great fit for this role or another role in our team.*

# SENIOR GEO-ENVIRONMENTAL ENGINEER
1. IGE Consulting
2. Careers
3. SENIOR GEO-ENVIRONMENTAL ENGINEER
### SENIOR GEO-ENVIRONMENTAL ENGINEER
Apply for this role
As we expand, there is an opportunity for a confident individual, passionate about the geo-environmental industry, looking to further their career in a senior role with our close-knit, dynamic team, reporting directly to director-level management. We pride ourselves on delivering excellent results for clients; this is only possible through the development and retention of highly skilled individuals with a shared goal in finding innovative, practical and cost-effective solutions.
The ideal individual for this role will be:
* At least 5 years into their career within the geo-environmental industry and confident in their abilities to work independently and part of a team;
* Comfortable in client-facing situations including business development meetings;
* Experienced in designing, organising and managing ground investigations utilising a range of intrusive techniques both for contaminated land and geotechnical purposes;
* Able to lead, manage and deliver technical projects, including preparing fee proposals and reports whilst understanding the financial implications of works;
* Familiar with validation and verification techniques and reporting of such techniques;
* Working towards chartership with a relevant professional body;
* Self-motivated and proactive, with demonstrable energy, drive and enthusiasm;
* Attentive to fine details across all work they produce;
* Capable of managing their own time to ensure deadlines are achieved;
* A pragmatic thinker capable of anticipating problems ahead of time and determining appropriate & cost-effective solutions; and
* Able to apply a commercial appraisal to projects, ensuring that value for money is paramount in all work undertaken.
Upon joining IGE Consulting, you will:
* Be encouraged and supported to progress professionally through refining your technical reporting skills and broadening your project experience; and
* Participate in a variety of challenging and innovative projects across residential, commercial and civil engineering industries, including having responsibility for project management, reporting and accounting through the entire life-cycle of a construction programme.
Your day to day responsibilities will include:
* Co-ordination, management, and where necessary, supervision, of ground investigations, including Phase 1 (desk-top) studies, Phase 2 (intrusive) investigations and subsequent monitoring and remediation works;
* Ensuring the highest standards of health and safety are followed during all field work practices;
* Authoring, reviewing and issuing of technical reports for clients including environmental risk assessments, remedial recommendations, foundation recommendations and coal mining risk assessments;
* Liaising with clients, subcontractors and staff in both office and field settings, including taking leadership roles within meetings; and
* Supervising and assisting junior staff with reports, drawings, models and fee proposals and mentoring them through their career development.
As a minimum, a full, clean Driving License and being based within an easily commutable distance to Manchester City Centre office are required.

# GRADUATE GEO-ENVIRONMENTAL ENGINEER
1. IGE Consulting
2. Careers
3. GRADUATE GEO-ENVIRONMENTAL ENGINEER
### GRADUATE GEO-ENVIRONMENTAL ENGINEER
Apply for this role
Due to on-going growth, there is an opportunity for a confident individual looking to kick-start their career in the geo-environmental industry to join our team. Upon joining IGE Consulting, you will:
* Become part of a close-knit and dynamic team focused on delivering excellent results for clients;
* Discover the fundamentals of the geo-environmental industry, including contaminated land risk assessment and geotechnical design;
* Be given the chance to learn and develop professionally in a practical, hands-on manner in both the office and our sites across the UK; and
* Participate in a variety of challenging and innovative projects across residential, commercial and civil engineering industries, including having opportunities to see projects through the entire life-cycle of a construction programme.
The ideal individual for this role will be:
* Confident working in a team and independently;
* Self-motivated and proactive, with demonstrable energy, drive and enthusiasm;
* Attentive to fine details across all work they produce;
* A pragmatic thinker capable of anticipating problems ahead of time and determining appropriate & cost-effective solutions;
* Willing to develop their proficiency in fieldwork techniques, production and management of data and both factual and interpretative reporting; and
* Able to develop an understanding of the commercial considerations associated with projects, with an appreciation of the importance of value for money.
Your day-to-day responsibilities will include:
* Co-ordination, supervision and management of ground investigations, including Phase 1 (desk-top) studies, Phase 2 (intrusive) investigations and subsequent monitoring and remediation works;
* Ensuring the highest standards of health and safety are followed during all field work practices;
* Accurate and precise recording of fieldwork data, and clear, concise presentation of such data;
* Liaising with clients, subcontractors and staff in both office and field settings;
* Preparing client reports, including environmental risk assessments, remedial recommendations, foundation recommendations and coal mining risk assessments; and
* Assisting senior staff with preparations of reports, drawings, models and fee
The minimum qualifications for this position are:
* First degree in Geology or related subject, ideally with practical modules encompassing field work;
* A full, clean Driving License;
* Based within an easily commutable distance to Manchester City Centre

Finance Business Partner - ICE - Industrial Cleaning Equipment # Finance Business Partner
**On-site**Finance, Admin & SystemsFull time
Totton, England, United Kingdom
OverviewApplication
## Description
This is an opportunity to provide meaningful financial information and analysis within a fast-growing, operationally complex service business looking to scale at pace.
ICE has seen substantial growth in the past 12 months. This growth will require more efficiency and automation across the business with a key focus on product and service profitability levels and cost control.
**Role Overview**
As Finance Business Partner, you will assist the CFO in driving shareholder value by analysing data to provide the Leadership Team and other stakeholders across the business with insightful, accurate, and timely financial information.
Due to the fast pace of growth the business is experiencing, there will be various opportunities to add additional value such as the implementation of a new ERP system and other ad-hoc strategic projects where financial modelling and analysis will be required.
This role would suit a commercially minded Accountant with 2-3 PQE in industry who can communicate confidently with stakeholders at all levels throughout the business.
**Key Responsibilities and Accountabilities:**
Financial Planning & Forecasting
* Lead the annual budget, quarterly re-forecast, and long-range planning processes;
* All forecasting models to include P&L, balance sheet, cashflow, and covenant projections per month;
Business Partnering
* Act as a trusted advisor to operational, sales, and back-office leadership teams;
* Translate financial and operational data into clear commercial insights and recommendations for stakeholders across the business including finding correlations and irregularities in data;
* Support strategic decision-making through scenario modelling and financial analysis;
Performance Reporting & Analysis
* Monitor and present monthly performance to budget with Departmental Heads discussing variances, owning any action plans to mitigate adverse variances to budget;
* Analyse revenue, gross profit and operating costs providing insightful analysis and improvement recommendations to the Leadership Team;
* Develop KPI dashboards and performance metrics for business leaders including Microsoft BI and within new ERP system.
Commercial & Operational Support
* Evaluate pricing strategies and customer profitability
* Support contract reviews, tender evaluations and business cases;
* Analyse labour costs, overheads, and operational performance metrics.
Strategic Projects and analysis
* Assist Project Manager during the implementation of new ERP system
* Conduct scenario planning, sensitivity analysis and investment appraisals;
* Develop financial business cases for capital expenditure and strategic projects;
Process Improvement & Governance
* Ensure consistency and integrity of financial data across the business;
* Drive automation and use of technology to enhance reporting and forecasting capability;
## Requirements
**Essential Experience, Skills and Qualifications:**
* Qualified accountant (ACA, ACCA, CIMA or equivalent);
* Minimum 3 years’ experience in Financial Planning & Analysis, Commercial Finance or Finance Business Partnering;
* Strong budgeting, forecasting and financial modelling experience including P&L, balance sheet, cashflow (direct and indirect) and covenant reporting;
* Advanced Microsoft Excel skills including macros, SQL reporting and automation of spreadsheets;
* Experience working with ERP systems and BI tools;
* Strong analytical and problem-solving capabilities;
* Excellent communication and stakeholder management skills;
* Ability to influence decision-making at senior management level;
* Commercially minded with strong business acumen.
**Desirable Technical Knowledge:**
* Knowledge of entire Microsoft stack including Excel, PowerPoint, Power BI and SharePoint;
* Experience within equipment sales, engineering, manufacturing or field service organisations;
* Knowledge of AI-driven forecasting, predictive analytics and business intelligence solutions;
* Experience leading finance transformation or process improvement projects.
## Benefits
* Competitive salary
* Private healthcare
* 21 + days annual leave plus bank holidays
* Enhanced workplace pension scheme
* Access to our discount and wellbeing portal, ICE Cube
* Life assurance which is 2x annual salary
* Bonus payment of £100.00 following 5 years’ service then an additional £25.00 for each subsequent year of service e.g. £125.00 following 6 years’ service
* Holiday buy back scheme
**About ICE**
With over 50 years of experience, ICE is the UK’s largest independent provider of cleaning equipment. We manage thousands of sites across the UK in a wide variety of sectors including retail, healthcare, warehousing, manufacturing, distribution, and education. As well as supplying and servicing traditional cleaning equipment, we also have over a decade of experience in robotic floor cleaning machines. We are not only committed to a greener future through our own ESG strategy, but we also place the utmost focus on ensuring we offer products and services to customers that support their own sustainability goals and commitments.
At ICE we strive to encourage personal development and career progression, offering on-the-job training as well as support for professional qualifications for our employees. We are a fast-growing business, and this position would suit someone who likes to hit the ground running and has a drive for success.
**How we do it:**
**But we’re still growing, and that’s why we need you.**
ICE is an equal-opportunity employer, and we’re on a mission to foster a diverse & inclusive workplace. Individuals seeking employment at ICE are considered without regard to race, religion, national origin, age, sex, gender, gender identity, gender expression, sexual orientation, marital status, medical condition, ancestry, physical or mental disability, military or veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law.
**Want to join our mission?**
If ICE sounds like the place to be to you, please apply using the link below.
Apply for this job

## Group Product Manager
Backbase
Product
Cardiff, UK
Posted on Aug 13, 2026
Apply now
As a Lead Product Manager – Digital Banking, you will define and drive the multi-year vision for our self-serve Digital Banking products. You’ll align this vision with our broader business banking strategy, build strong business cases to secure resources, and lead the execution to ensure market success.
This role requires a mix of strategic thinking, stakeholder engagement, and team leadership. You’ll work closely with bank executives, customers, and internal teams to translate needs into actionable product strategies while mentoring and guiding other Product Managers to success. Your goal? Deliver measurable business impact—acquiring new clients, increasing ARR, reducing churn, and enabling upsell/cross-sell opportunities.
## What you'll do
* 1. Product Strategy & Roadmap Development
* Define and execute the multi-year vision for Backbase’s Digital Banking offerings, leveraging existing solutions and accelerating innovation;
* Develop compelling business cases for major initiatives, securing investment and prioritization for high-impact projects. 2. Stakeholder & Executive Engagement
* Partner with C-level executives, banking leaders, and customers to understand market needs and translate them into actionable product requirements;
* Work cross-functionally with R&D, engineering, UX, and business teams to ensure smooth execution and timely delivery;
* Align product strategy with wider company objectives, influencing decision-making at all levels. 3. Leadership & Team Development
* Mentor and coach mid-level Product Managers and Business Analysts, ensuring alignment with organizational goals;
* Foster a collaborative, innovative, and accountable team culture that thrives on excellence. 4. Driving Measurable Outcomes
* Deliver results that directly impact key metrics:
* New customer acquisition;
* Increased ARR (Annual Recurring Revenue);
* Reduced customer churn;
* Higher upsell and cross-sell opportunities.
## Who you are
* Experience & Skills
* Digital Banking Expertise: Strong background in Digital Banking domains, with prior experience in Payments being a significant advantage;
* Product Development: 5+ years of experience leading cross-functional Agile teams to deliver successful digital products in scale-up or enterprise environments;
* Strategic Vision: Proven ability to define and execute a 2-3 year product strategy that aligns with company objectives and drives measurable business impact;
* Market Leader: Experience influencing product direction through market insights, competitive analysis, and innovation, with a track record of driving industry-leading initiatives;
* Team Development: Demonstrated experience mentoring and developing product teams, with at least 2+ direct reports or a history of coaching junior PMs to senior roles;
* Customer-Centric Mindset: Strong ability to translate customer insights into product decisions, with a proven track record of improving key metrics such as NPS, engagement, or retention by 10-20%;
* Agile Expertise: Hands-on experience in Agile environments, managing products with 100k+ users or $10M+ in revenue;
* Commercial Acumen: Strong understanding of sales and product marketing dynamics, with the ability to act as a Subject Matter Expert to guide product development. Personal Attributes
* Passionate & Self-Driven: You thrive in fast-paced environments, pushing for clarity and delivery while maintaining strong collaboration;
* Strategic Thinker: You possess a distinctive ability to prioritize and delegate tasks effectively, balancing varying workloads and importance;
* Adaptable Leader: You navigate ambiguity with ease and rapidly adapt to shifting priorities;
* Role Model: You lead by example, demonstrating the behaviors, work ethic, and commitment that inspire your team to excel. Why Join Backbase? At Backbase, we don’t just build products—we shape the future of digital banking. As a Lead Product Manager, you will drive the evolution of our Digital Banking strategy, with a strong focus on payment modernization as a key pillar of transformation. This role is your opportunity to redefine how banks innovate, ensuring seamless, frictionless experiences that meet the growing demands of businesses and consumers. You’ll work closely with C-level executives, banking leaders, and cross-functional teams to develop solutions that accelerate digital banking adoption, modernize payment infrastructure, and drive measurable business impact. We celebrate bold ideas, collaboration, and innovation—and we have fun doing it. Join us, and let’s redefine the digital banking landscape together.

# Cybercrime Analyst (12 Month Placement Opportunity)
Bath
**About Netcraft**
Netcraft is the global leader in cybercrime detection and disruption. We’re a trusted partner for three of the four largest companies in the world and many large governments. We've blocked over 225 million cyber-attacks to date, and we take down around 33% of the world's phishing attacks.
Our purpose and passion are focused on just one thing: protecting the world from cybercrime.
That passion shapes how we work, too. We’re proud of our talented team and the value each person brings, and we’ve built a workplace where people feel supported and inspired. From strong benefits and wellness programs to meaningful collaboration and team connection.
**The role** We are seeking Cybercrime Analyst Interns to join our Technical Operations team for 12 months. Cybercrime Analyst roles at Netcraft are an opportunity to make a real difference in the world by identifying threats and acting to protect governments, banks, and consumers from online attacks. You will be a key part of the incident response team, finding innovative ways to rapidly disrupt cyber-attacks against Netcraft's large and prestigious client base. Day to day, your responsibilities will include:
* Cybercrime incident response – communicating analysis of cyber threats to relevant parties in order to mitigate attacks;
* Classification of malicious websites, social media profiles, apps, emails, and phone numbers;
* Providing clear and professional feedback to customers on incidents and classifications;
* Sharing your ideas on how to improve processes and workflows.
Based at our Bath office, but with hybrid flexibility, you’ll report directly to a Technical Operations Team Lead and will work closely with colleagues across different teams. The reward package:
* A salary of £28,000 for the duration of your 12-month placement
* An excellent range of benefits including:
+ Hybrid and flexible working
+ 33 days holiday per year, prorated to the duration of your role
+ Pension scheme membership with 5% employer contributions
+ Free meals, drinks and snacks provided daily in the offices
+ Comprehensive wellness provisions
+ Regular events such as monthly board game nights, quarterly socials and a big summer party
To be successful, you’ll need:
* Attention to detail, adaptability and strong intellectual and commercial curiosity;
* A positive, helpful and solutions-focused approach;
* Interest in the internet and cybercrime prevention;
* Excellent communication skills with a high standard of written English;
* Ability to engage with people in a warm, helpful, and professional way;
* Self-motivation, ability to take initiative, and work as part of a team;
* Aptitude for analysing and using technical information;
* Competence in handling incoming phone calls;
* Determination, enthusiasm, and a solutions-focused approach;
* Some experience in cybersecurity is useful but not essential as full training will be provided.
Your standard working days will be Monday to Friday. We also have a rota system for limited weekend and evening working - because Netcraft protects its customers 24/7, 365 days per year - which we'll discuss with you at interview. We warmly welcome candidates from any and every walk of life. Even if you’re not sure you can tick all the boxes above, please do apply – we review every application with real interest. We’re also happy to adjust our hiring process to ensure that candidates with special needs or disabilities can participate just as fully and comfortably as anyone else. **Note for sandwich placement students:** Before you apply you must check with placements staff in your academic department to make sure this placement is appropriate for your degree programme. Historically, we have had many STEM students do this role.
